# =============================================================================
# Core package set for the Iris desktop image.
#
# Two consumers:
#   * live-build: config/package-lists/*.list.chroot  (this file, as-is)
#   * scripts/install.sh --packages  (reads the same list, ignoring comments)
#
# Every name below was checked against the Debian 13 (trixie) archive. Removed
# from the previous revision because they do not exist and broke `lb build`:
#   plymouth-theme-iris   -> no such package anywhere; a Plymouth theme is not
#                            a drop-in asset and a bad one can hang boot.
#   gpaste                -> a clipboard *manager* (needs a shell extension, and
#                            it is not part of a themed desktop); it also pulls
#                            in gnome-shell bits.
#
# xwayland is REQUIRED for the Wayland session: cinnamon-common ships the
# session without depending on it, and without it nemo-desktop dies with
# "Cannot open display" giving a black desktop (Debian bug #1147594).
# =============================================================================

# Cinnamon core (shell + Muffin WM + Nemo + settings)
cinnamon-core
cinnamon-l10n

# Display manager + greeter (LightDM keeps the session picker simple and X11+WL friendly)
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter

# X server and input
xorg
xserver-xorg-video-all
xserver-xorg-input-all

# Wayland plumbing for the "Iris (Wayland)" session
xwayland

# Icon + cursor themes referenced by theme/Iris/index.theme
papirus-icon-theme
bibata-cursor-theme

# Settings backend used by scripts/apply-settings.sh
dconf-cli
gsettings-desktop-schemas
xdg-user-dirs

# Network stack + tray applet (the network@cinnamon.org applet expects these)
network-manager
# nm-applet ships inside network-manager-gnome — there is no Debian package
# called `nm-applet` (the old list named one, which failed the image build).
network-manager-gnome

# Iris itself is NOT in Debian: build it (`make deb`) and drop the .deb into
# config/packages.chroot/ — live-build installs *.deb from there. The hook
# config/hooks/05-iris-defaults.chroot bakes the gsettings profile into the
# image's system dconf db.

# Firmware for a first boot on real laptops (needs archive-areas to include
# non-free-firmware in `lb config`)
firmware-misc-nonfree
